Abbreviation:
  LeanWang.Abstract.Direction is
    (Fin 4).

Abbreviation:
  LeanWang.Abstract.n is
    (0 : Direction).

Abbreviation:
  LeanWang.Abstract.s is
    (1 : Direction).

Abbreviation:
  LeanWang.Abstract.e is
    (2 : Direction).

Abbreviation:
  LeanWang.Abstract.w is
    (3 : Direction).

Abbreviation:
  LeanWang.Abstract.Tile is
    Direction → ℕ.

Definition:
  a list T of Tile elements is LeanWang.Abstract.TilesPlane if
    there is a function t from ℤ and ℤ to Tile such that
      for all integers x and y:
        t x y ∈ T and t x y e = t (x + 1) y w and t x y n = t x (y + 1) s.

Definition:
  LeanWang.Abstract.CoRE is
    the function mapping an implicit element α of Type u_1 and an instance of typeclass Primcodable α and a function p from α to Prop to
      (the function mapping an element «a» of α to
        «a» is not p) is recursively enumerable.

Definition:
  LeanWang.Abstract.CoREComplete is
    the function mapping an implicit element α of Type u_1 and an instance of typeclass Primcodable α and a function p from α to Prop to
      p is CoRE and (for every function q from ℕ to Prop:
        if q is CoRE then
          there is a function r from ℕ to α such that
            r is computable and (for every natural number n:
              n is q if and only if (r n) is p)).

Theorem LeanWang.Abstract.coRE_complete:
  TilesPlane is CoREComplete

Theorem LeanWang.Abstract.undecidable:
  TilesPlane is not computable
